h strengths and concerns:\n\nA:\n- Strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities.\n- Concerns: unfriendly, unhealthy eating, show-off behavior, not good at taking criticism, unorganized.\n\nB:\n- Strengths: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills.\n- Concerns: pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, nasty remarks toward colleagues, weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy).\n\nC:\n- Strengths: can make correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis, 100% reliable, creates positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention skills.\n- Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education.\n\nD:\n- Strengths: takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, can concentrate very well, responds to unexpected events adequately.\n- Concerns: hot temper, know-it-all (arrogant), weak leadership, moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nNow evaluate against criteria:\n\nOperational reliability: A? Not mentioned reliability; B conscientious suggests reliability; C 100% reliable; D responsibility suggests reliability.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well; C calm in crisis; D responds to unexpected events adequately; A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B good at weather assessment, computer skills; C quick decisions, attention; D problem solving, concentration.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions; A anticipates dangerous situations; D problem solving; B good weather assessment.\n\nAttention/accuracy: B weak memory for numbers; C excellent attention; D concentration; A unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: A unfriendly, show-off; B pretentious, wrong tone, nasty remarks; C creates positive atmosphere but egocentric; D hot temper, loner.\n\nProfessional communication: A unfriendly; B wrong tone; C difficulty communicating; D arrogant.\n\nResponsibility/maturity: D takes responsibility seriously; B conscientious; A leadership; C reliability.\n\nAdaptability/feedback: A not good at taking criticism; B pretentious; C not willing to further education; D know-it-all.\n\nOverall, C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, calmness, crew atmosphere, attention. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Those are serious but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks and D's hot temper. A has strong anticipation and leadership but interpersonal issues and unorganized.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? C seems balanced: reliability, decision quality, calmness, crew atmosphere, attention. Communication difficulty and egocentric could affect crew cooperation, but he creates positive atmosphere. Egocentric may be mitigated. Not willing to further education could be a concern for long-term development but maybe less immediate.\n\nThus perhaps C is the best overall. However Anna argued for A, Markus for D, Sofia originally for B. Now we need to converge. As Sofia, we can reconsider and perhaps shift to C, citing its strengths and that concerns are manageable. Or we could keep B if we think stress handling is crucial. But C also calm in crisis, which is stress resilience.\n\nGiven the evidence, I think C is strongest overall. So Sofia should change vote to Candidate C, providing reasoning.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention that while B's stress handling is good, his communication issues and weak numeric memory are serious; D's responsibility is good but hot temper is severe; A's anticipation is valuable but his interpersonal issues are significant; C's combination of quick correct decisions, calmness, reliability, and positive crew atmosphere outweigh his communication difficulty, which can be trained.\n\nThus we vote for C.\n\nNow produce public message and metadata JSON."}
