bution, referencing prior discussion, using explicit facts, and give a vote. We need to decide whether to keep our vote for A, shift to C, D, or B. We need to consider the evidence and try to converge.\n\nCurrent votes: Agent 1 (Anna) currently voted A (in round 2). Agent 2 (Markus) voted D. Agent 3 (Sofia) voted C. So we have three different votes. We need to respond now. We should either keep A or shift. We need to consider the arguments: Sofia argued C is best due to decision quality, calmness, reliability, crew atmosphere, attention, and manageable concerns. Markus argued D is best due to responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handling unexpected events, with concerns manageable. Anna argued A is best due to anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, with concerns manageable.\n\nWe need to evaluate which candidate best meets criteria overall. Let's weigh:\n\n- Reliability: C is 100% reliable. D takes responsibility seriously (implies reliability). B is conscientious (reliable). A not mentioned reliability.\n\n- Stress resilience: B handles stress well, C calm in crisis, D responds to unexpected events adequately, A unknown.\n\n- Technical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B good at weather assessment, computer skills; C quick correct decisions; D solves problems extremely well, concentration.\n\n- Decision quality: C quick correct decisions; A anticipates dangerous situations; D solves problems; B good weather assessment.\n\n- Attention/accuracy: C excellent attention; D concentration; B weak memory for numbers; A unknown.\n\n- Crew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere; D hot tempered, loner; B nasty remarks, uncooperative; A unfriendly, show-off.\n\n- Professional communication: C difficulty communicating; D arrogant; B wrong tone; A unfriendly.\n\n- Responsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; B conscientious; C reliability; A leadership.\n\n- Adaptability/feedback: A not good at criticism; B pretentious; C not willing further education; D know-it-all.\n\nOverall, C seems strongest on reliability, decision quality, calmness, attention, crew atmosphere (positive). Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing further education. Those are concerns but perhaps less severe than D's hot temper and arrogance, B's nasty remarks, A's unfriendly and show-off.\n\nThus I think we should shift to Candidate C. As Anna, we can say after hearing arguments, I now see C as best overall. Provide reasoning referencing prior points and evidence.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: Should be concise, refer to prior discussion, mention evidence, explain why C is best, and state recommendation.\n\nThen METADATA_JSON: {\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}\n\nProceed."}
